[{:db/id "79b7ae4b-a531-5e36-9642-7063e55bfd39" :answer/id #uuid "79b7ae4b-a531-5e36-9642-7063e55bfd39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ef7b0bc1-b548-5a45-8603-72e62b1d2cfa" :answer/id #uuid "ef7b0bc1-b548-5a45-8603-72e62b1d2cfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4f303671-2e9e-5abb-8d28-bb66030b781a" :answer/id #uuid "4f303671-2e9e-5abb-8d28-bb66030b781a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d73fd73f-0590-5f6f-a4f5-edc9dba1df7a" :answer/id #uuid "d73fd73f-0590-5f6f-a4f5-edc9dba1df7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5ac71fd6-aef4-521a-be30-ea15e9fd1d7e" :answer/id #uuid "5ac71fd6-aef4-521a-be30-ea15e9fd1d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8e1dbdc3-6266-50e7-8ca0-341d52ae8cbe" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1dbdc3-6266-50e7-8ca0-341d52ae8cbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["79b7ae4b-a531-5e36-9642-7063e55bfd39" "ef7b0bc1-b548-5a45-8603-72e62b1d2cfa" "4f303671-2e9e-5abb-8d28-bb66030b781a" "d73fd73f-0590-5f6f-a4f5-edc9dba1df7a" "5ac71fd6-aef4-521a-be30-ea15e9fd1d7e"] :answer-field/correct "4f303671-2e9e-5abb-8d28-bb66030b781a" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3f24b968-c90a-5088-b77c-2d14ff47db8f" :question/id #uuid "3f24b968-c90a-5088-b77c-2d14ff47db8f" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{8}=\\cos\\theta,\\quad \\frac{y}{2}=\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $\\cos\\theta$ term in the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{8} & =\\cos\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(8)^{2}} & =\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64} & =\\cos^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $\\sin\\theta$ term in the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2} & =\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2)^{2}} & =\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =\\sin^2\\theta.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["8e1dbdc3-6266-50e7-8ca0-341d52ae8cbe"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "4a4eed1f-3af9-5976-b03d-acebc6d144a3" :answer/id #uuid "4a4eed1f-3af9-5976-b03d-acebc6d144a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c21af765-fb6e-5349-8e2a-df0c6bd18fc6" :answer/id #uuid "c21af765-fb6e-5349-8e2a-df0c6bd18fc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{121}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cc606102-32d8-5ce3-b21a-bb23f9b354a3" :answer/id #uuid "cc606102-32d8-5ce3-b21a-bb23f9b354a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{11}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "eb71c85d-2053-5194-ac88-087d8dcd6991" :answer/id #uuid "eb71c85d-2053-5194-ac88-087d8dcd6991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{121}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "94334901-fb74-5742-be6c-6a327b7ee13e" :answer/id #uuid "94334901-fb74-5742-be6c-6a327b7ee13e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure :answ